WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.260
So I'm Michela Massimi
I'm a professor of philosophy of science at University of Edinburgh.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:14.559
So my lecture at the Royal society is entitled why the philosophy of science matters to

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:17.410
science.
Now the philosophy of science should

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:21.160
matter to science is not a foregone
conclusion and philosophy of science has

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:26.590
often been the target of bad press among
scientists dismissive claims in my view

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:30.550
originate from widespread and the
misguided assumption namely that

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:35.140
philosophy of science has to be of use
to scientists otherwise it's no use at

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:40.930
all. In reply I would like to say that
philosophy of science like any other

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:46.179
fields in humanities is valuable and
it's valuable to ask why humankind's

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:50.190
they have a very sophisticated
scientific history and cultural heritage

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:56.350
we build narratives about science we
like to scrutinize modeling practices

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.469
and methodology in science because it's
it's part of our knowledge it's of our

00:01:02.469 --> 00:01:06.940
tradition and moreover philosophy
science plays an important social

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:12.580
function and media coverage and public
discourse on science is often

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:18.430
intertwined with controversies stirred
by political lobbyists and it is the job

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.810
of scientists in those cases to find the
evidence and the scientific facts but

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:28.060
it's equally the job of philosophers of
science to work alongside scientists and

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:33.160
to stand up for science and build the
narratives about issues such as evidence

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:37.840
and the natural natural progress and
truth and realism and pluralism in

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.410
science because those narratives
ultimately matter they matter to us

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:47.610
and they matter to political
decision-making and the public policy.

